# The control for the animated Restless Anchorage: here Bot1 never animates it, so the tapped Anchorage is only a land when Split Up's
# first mode resolves (destroy all tapped creatures) and it stays, as do the tapped Moxen. Its owner's tapped Ornithopter dies
# (crewing is not needed: Bot1 attacks with it on turn 3, and it is still tapped in the second main phase).

[Bot1 Deck]
Restless Anchorage
Black Lotus
Split Up
Plains
Ornithopter
Plains x2
Plains x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x18

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Restless Anchorage.Play
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Split Up.Cast
Bot1.Modes(1)

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot1.Graveyard = Split Up; Ornithopter; Black Lotus
Bot1.Battlefield = Restless Anchorage; Plains
